519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Peter England is a prominent Indian menswear brand that serves as a fascinating case study in navigating local identity versus global aspirations. Though often seen as a global brand, its journey is deeply connected to the Indian consumer, making it a prime example of glocalization. The brand's success is largely due to its strategy of thinking globally but acting locally. By blending global aspirations with local realities, Peter England has establishe a strong presence in the dynamic Indian market.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Despite its global facade, Peter England's core market and roots are firmly in India. The brand is part of Aditya Birla Fashion and Retail Ltd. \(ABFRL\), a major Indian fashion conglomerate. Its product development, pricing, and distribution networks are specifically tailored to the Indian consumer's preferences and purchasing power)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
521 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (It has effectively cultivated an image of global appeal. The brand name itself evokes a sense of European heritage and classic style. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [12 13]
>>
endobj
522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Its collections frequently mirror international fashion trends, and marketing campaigns project a modern, aspirational masculinity that appeals to a globally-aware audience. This strategic branding enables Peter England to compete with international players within the Indian market.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
endobj
523 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In India, Peter England has strategically positioned itself as an affordable premium brand, making fashion accessible to a broader audience. This pricing strategy is vital in a market where value for money is a key consumer driver. The brand's extensive retail presence across Tier 1, 2, and 3 cities highlights its commitment to reaching consumers throughout India.  Marketing campaigns often feature Indian models and settings, with messaging that connects with the aspirations and cultural nuances of the Indian male, creating a strong local connection.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [10 11]
>>
endobj
524 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 154 0 R
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
525 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Peter England's strategy leverages the prestige of a "global" brand while ensuring its products are relevant and accessible to the Indian consumer. The brand operates in the fiercely competitive Indian apparel market, facing challenges from both international giants and strong local players. Its ability to continue balancing global trends with local insights through its glocal approach will be crucial for its future growth and leadership in the Indian menswear segment.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
