665 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Consumer loyalty is shaped more by the relevance and quality of a product than its origin. People usually stick with brands that meet their needs and deliver consistent value. However, origin does hold importance in certain cases. For example, in whiskies or Scotch, authenticity of origin greatly influences consumer preference. Similarly, with mangoes, one may enjoy the fruit generally but still choose favorites like Alphonso, Hapus, or Ratnagiri. So while origin can matter in specific categories, quality and relevance remain the stronger drivers of loyalty.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
